  28:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *
  29:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * \defgroup IfxLld_Egtm_Pwm_Usage How to use the PWM Interface layer?
  30:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * \ingroup IfxLld_Egtm_Pwm
  31:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * \section IfxLld_Egtm_Pwm_Overview Overview
  32:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * This documentation describes the usage of PWM driver interface layer of GTM/eGTM module present 
  33:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * This interface can be used to generate upto 16 PWM signals (8 of them can be complementary pairs
  34:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * Users can pass an array of channel configurations. The first channel acts as "Base" channel and 
  35:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * The base channel is responsible for controlling the frequency of all channels. It does so by gen
  36:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * The synchronous channels receive and forward this trigger to subsequent channels. The trigger no
  37:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * <b>Note:</b>
  38:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# This documentation will use the term "GTM" to mean both "GTM" and "EGTM" module unless sp
  39:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# Enabling of Gtm module and configuration of clock is not supported by this driver.
  40:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# PWM driver can configure only one cluster and one submodule (Tom/Atom) at a time
  41:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# Atom has only 8 channels so at max 8 complementary PWM signal pairs can be generated when
  42:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# If channels span across two TGCs in Tom, then driver uses TBU channel 0 to start the chan
  43:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * \subsection IfxLld_Egtm_Pwm_Overview_Func Functionalities Provided
  44:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * The PWM interface layer provides the following functionalities:
  45:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# Usage of TOM/ATOM submodule for PWM generation
  46:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# Generation of edge and center aligned PWM signals
  47:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# Usage of upto 16 channels (1 base + 15 synchronous channels with contiguous channel numbe
  48:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# Generation of upto 2 PWM output signals from each channel (depending on DTM Availability)
  49:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# Static and run time APIs for configuring PWM frequency, duty, phase (edge aligned), and d
  50:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *         -# Synchronous update of one channel
  51:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *         -# Immediate update of one channel
  52:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *         -# Synchronous update of all channels
  53:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *         -# Immediate update of all channels
  54:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * \subsection IfxLld_Egtm_Pwm_Init Interface Initialization
  55:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * Initialization can be done by calling IfxEgtm_Pwm_init() function.\n
  56:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  * The function performs the following steps:
  57:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# Retrieves clock information for Atom/Tom and DTM
  58:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *     -# Initializes base and sync channels:
  59:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *         -# Saves pointers to registers for faster access later
  60:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *         -# Configures Atom/Tom global control and channel registers
  61:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *         -# Configures Pwm alignment of each channel
  62:../Libraries/iLLD/TC4xx/CpuGeneric/Egtm/Pwm/IfxEgtm_Pwm.h ****  *         -# Configures Base channel with Pwm frequency and to generate trigger at end of period
